{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789917938,"nonce":"IJq/wKz1SS+2PZeuTaDQYMvuk8w=","message":"Root cause, found 2026-09-20: not the collector. The interpreter kept a\nfallback store for HVIRTUAL fields, `virtual_fields: HashMap\u003c(address,\nfield), NanBoxedValue\u003e`, used whenever `OField`/`OSetField` hit a virtual\nwhose `value` is non-null -- a view made by `hl_to_virtual`. utest's\n`Assert.same` passes its `status` object to `sameAs` as such a view, and\n`status.path` went through the map on every array element.\n\nTwo defects in that map. It held GC pointers the collector could not see\n(Rust heap, no root), and it was keyed by object address and never\ninvalidated, so a new virtual at an address an old one had occupied read\nthe old entry back. The crashing read was `status.path` returning a\nString freed 25 collections earlier; the memory had since been handed to\na `ValueType` enum, a `utest.Dispatcher`, whatever the layout put there,\nwhich is why the fault site moved with every change to the binary and\nwhy every collector audit passed: at the collection that freed it, the\nString was genuinely unreachable.\n\nFix: read and write virtual fields through the field pointer table after\nthe `vvirtual` header, as HashLink and ash's Cranelift tier do; a null\nentry, or a method field on a view, goes to the dynamic accessors by\nhash. The map is deleted.\n\nReproducer: `ASH_GC_GEN=0 ASH_GC_TRIGGER_MB=4096\nASH_GC_COLLECT_AT_REFILLS=every:3 ash --mode interp bin/unit.hl --ash-only\nunit.TestRest` (every:2 and every:5 for other layouts); `ASH_GC_STALE=1`\nturns the segfault into `STALE: r12 read for field 1 in String.__add__ ...\ncontaining allocation start 0x..., written at collection 35, line recycled\nat 35` with the frames' registers. Before the fix: STALE in 3/3 on the\ncrashing arm. After: 0/6 arms, whole-suite interp 24/24 with majors only\nand 24/24 with ASH_GC_GEN=1, conformance per-case on all four engines\nunchanged.\n\nNew switches, documented in docs/debugging.md: ASH_GC_STALE,\nASH_GC_CHECK_FRESH (shadow owner table: memory handed out twice),\nASH_GC_STACK_ONLY, ASH_GC_VERIFY_HEAP, ASH_INTERP_CHECK_FRAMES, and\n`every:N` / `a-b` forms for ASH_GC_COLLECT_AT_REFILLS. ASH_GC_POISON now\nalso poisons recycled line runs.\n\n\nFixed in ca2f918.","files":null}]}